# TODO - Parametric compiler challenge generator

## Objective

Build deterministic workload generators whose difficulty can grow continuously
instead of saturating at one application-specific threshold. Generate families
covering arithmetic and ternary transforms, expression DAGs, control flow,
function calls, memory pressure, pointer/alias patterns admitted by the C
profile, streaming state machines, graph problems, layout pressure, Malbolge
self-modification, block synthesis, and whole-program compositions with known
semantic oracles. Every instance is identified by family, version, seed, target
profile, and explicit difficulty parameters so two algorithms can be compared on
exactly the same problem rather than on vaguely similar examples.

**Current implementation.**

- `benchmarks/challenges/generate.py` implements deterministic
  `arithmetic-dag/v1`, `linear-mix/v1`, `branch-mix/v1`,
  `memory-walk/v1`, `call-chain/v1`, `pointer-walk/v1`, `alias-walk/v1`, and
  `stream-state/v1`, `graph-reduce/v1`, `layout-chain/v1`, and
  `ternary-fold/v1` challenges identified by family, version, unsigned seed,
  canonical target-profile fingerprint, and node count. Every node feeds the
  next node on a live dependency spine so difficulty cannot grow through dead C
  statements. The domain-separated linear family is a strict predecessor
  chain while the DAG family retains additional source-order fan-in. The
  branch family adds one live `if`/`else` diamond per node. The memory family
  uses a fixed eight-cell local array with deterministic indexed read/write/read
  operations per node. The call family threads the live value through one pure
  three-argument helper call per node.
- Each identity emits `program.c`, `oracle.bin`, and canonical `manifest.json`
  bytes. The manifest binds source/oracle SHA-256 digests, while the source
  entry
  `malbolge_challenge` returns the full oracle `uint32_t` without unavailable
  guest libc calls.
- Analysis evidence locks byte-identical replay, hash-locked
  `arithmetic-dag/v1` and `pointer-walk/v1` vectors, difficulty growth for all
  eleven topologies,
  invalid identity rejection, non-destructive no-replace publication including a
  raced
  final-path collision, ABI/libc admission, and pinned-Clang agreement between
  emitted C and the independent Python oracle for all eleven families. The
  normalized frontend additionally preserves the branch family’s expected
  `if-statement` count, the memory family’s exact array-subscript count, and
  one helper call per call-family node. `pointer-walk/v1` selects one array
  slot from the live value through a local pointer on every node; normalized
  frontend evidence retains one runtime-dependent subscript, one pointer
  declaration, and address/read/write unary operations per node. `alias-walk/v1`
  adds two runtime-selected pointers per node; those pointers may alias the same
  cell and the independent oracle preserves the emitted sequential write order.
  `stream-state/v1` uses `nodes` as deterministic stream length under a
  seed-stable transition rule, retaining one live `for` loop, one indexed token
  read, and one state-dependent branch in normalized frontend evidence.
  `graph-reduce/v1` generates one acyclic parent link and weight per vertex;
  runtime reduction keeps parent-index and predecessor-state dependencies live,
  with normalized evidence retaining one loop and six graph/state subscripts.
  `layout-chain/v1` emits one distinct live helper function and call target per
  node, so function/code-layout pressure grows without dead source blocks;
  normalized evidence retains `nodes + 2` functions and `nodes + 1` calls.
  `ternary-fold/v1` keeps state and tokens inside the classic ten-trit domain
  and performs explicit base-three quotient/remainder mixing before folding the
  node-scaled token stream; native evidence matches the Python oracle.
- The objective remains open: larger-stress and broader workload families plus
  the required end-to-end compiled/executed Malbolge fixture are not yet
  implemented.

## Acceptance

- Every challenge has stable family/version/seed/profile identity, an oracle,
  and difficulty parameters that can scale beyond trivial saturation while
  remaining reproducible.
- The end-to-end fixture demonstrates the intended behavior from admitted
  source/input through the actual generated/executed Malbolge path.
- The work states a falsifiable question or hypothesis, an explicit baseline,
  and an observation that would reject or materially weaken the proposed
  technique before performance conclusions are accepted.
- If executable algorithm research is required, the stable ID is mirrored under
  `docs/research/algorithms/<id>/` and `algorithms/<id>/`; ordinary product
  engineering is not forced into that mirror.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

